40
00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.500
Now we're gonna go in here into the objects

41
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.359
and then into the home and kitchen

42
00:01:41.359 --> 00:01:42.939
and finally accessories.

43
00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:44.599
And I just know this is where this is at

44
00:01:44.599 --> 00:01:45.859
that I'm looking for.

45
00:01:45.859 --> 00:01:47.379
I'm gonna look for that knife block.

46
00:01:47.379 --> 00:01:53.250
So go ahead up here and type in knife block.

47
00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.170
And you should see this little guy here.

48
00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.530
And all you have to do is grab it

49
00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:58.870
and position it here into the scene,

50
00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:01.170
just like this, okay?

51
00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.769
And it will drag it in.

52
00:02:02.769 --> 00:02:04.849
Now you'll notice it snaps right to the top.

53
00:02:04.849 --> 00:02:06.310
Now there are some cool ways.

54
00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:07.730
Now you see how this turns orange?

55
00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.430
I'm gonna zoom in a little bit.

56
00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:10.270
This turns orange.

57
00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.569
What this does is this allows you to snap along the edge.

58
00:02:13.569 --> 00:02:15.330
Now you'll notice it just kind of floats

59
00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.189
right along that plane.

60
00:02:17.189 --> 00:02:18.449
It won't go any place else

61
00:02:18.449 --> 00:02:20.090
as long as you have it there.

62
00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.210
Now see the little globe here?

63
00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:24.650
This enables you to snap wherever.

64
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:26.849
Obviously you don't want it to go on the side of a wall,

65
00:02:26.849 --> 00:02:28.050
but that's the power of this

66
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.930
to say like for a picture, for example,

67
00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:31.770
you could snap it to the wall.

68
00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:32.770
But in this case, we're gonna go ahead

69
00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:35.229
and snap it right to our surface here

70
00:02:35.229 --> 00:02:36.770
and drag it along.

71
00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:37.729
And then we're gonna rotate.

72
00:02:37.729 --> 00:02:39.650
Now see how this turns into orange?

73
00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:41.370
You can actually type in your values.

74
00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.830
So let's just say you wanna do a 90 degree.

75
00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.849
There, bam.

76
00:02:44.849 --> 00:02:47.650
Or let's say, hey, maybe I wanted another 90 degrees

77
00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:48.969
or 180.

78
00:02:48.969 --> 00:02:51.039
You could type in 180.

79
00:02:51.039 --> 00:02:51.879
And there we go.

80
00:02:51.879 --> 00:02:53.900
It's kind of facing the direction that I wanted it.

81
00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.879
Now, if you still feel like this isn't positioned

82
00:02:55.879 --> 00:02:58.439
exactly where you would want it, that's okay.

83
00:02:58.439 --> 00:02:59.960
Play around with that.

84
00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.439
I'm also gonna have you play around

85
00:03:01.439 --> 00:03:03.740
with to add some additional type of objects

86
00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:05.520
